  "explanation" : "Compute server 1 (server-1) is the lowest of the three removable server chassis in the accepted rack. Its compute role represents running applications and processing data; processors, memory, cooling, and power components are not modeled inside it in this scene.\n\nThe network switch (switch), positioned above the servers, represents the equipment that connects them to the network. In a typical setup, server-1 sends and receives data through a network interface connected to the switch, which forwards traffic toward other connected devices or an upstream network. The server performs computation; the switch provides network connectivity.\n\nBoth are children of the rack assembly. This snapshot shows no cables or explicit connection records, so their networking relationship is illustrative, not a verified physical link or configured topology. No geometry changes are proposed.",
